@article{ WOS:001206086300001,
Author = {Ferguson, Laura and Emoto, Sarah and Gruskin, Sofia},
Title = {Laws governing access to sexual health services and information:
   contents, protections, and restrictions},
Journal = {SEXUAL AND REPRODUCTIVE HEALTH MATTERS},
Year = {2024},
Volume = {32},
Number = {1},
Month = {DEC 31},
Abstract = {Access to sexual health services and information is critical to
   achieving the highest attainable standard of sexual health, and enabling
   legal environments are key to advancing progress in this area. In
   determining overall alignment with human rights standards to respect,
   protect, and fulfil sexual health-related rights without discrimination,
   there are many aspects of laws, including their specificity and content,
   which impact which sexual health services and information are availed,
   which are restricted, and for whom. To understand the nature of existing
   legal provisions surrounding access to sexual health services and
   information, we analysed the content of 40 laws in English, French, and
   Spanish from 18 countries for the specific sexual health services and
   information to which access is ensured or prohibited, and the
   non-discrimination provisions within these laws. Overall, there was wide
   variation across countries in the types of laws covering these services
   and the types and number of services and information ensured. Some
   countries covered different services through multiple laws, and most of
   the laws dedicated specifically to sexual health addressed only a narrow
   aspect of sexual health and covered a small range of services. The
   protected characteristics in non-discrimination provisions and the
   specificity of these provisions with regard to sexual health services
   also varied. Findings may inform national legal and policy dialogues
   around sexual health to identify opportunities for positive change, as
   well as to guide further investigation to understand the relationship
   between such legal provisions, the implementation of these laws within
   countries, and relevant sexual health outcomes.
   Access to sexual health services and information is important to being
   able to have good sexual health. Laws are relevant because what they
   include and how specific they are affects what types of sexual health
   services people can access, what types of services are illegal, and
   whether or not all people can access services equally. We reviewed 40
   laws in English, French, and Spanish from 18 countries to understand how
   many and which sexual health services and information countries ensure
   in their laws, which sexual health services are illegal, and which
   people are protected from discrimination in accessing these services. We
   found that countries use many different types of laws to ensure access
   to sexual health services or information, and most countries do not
   cover the same types or number of sexual health services. There are also
   differences in which people are specifically protected from
   discrimination in the laws we reviewed. These findings are important
   because they may help countries identify ways that access to sexual
   health services and information could be improved so as to improve
   people's sexual health. They may also guide future research.
   L'acc \& egrave;s aux services et \& agrave; l'information en mati \&
   egrave;re de sant \& eacute; sexuelle est capital pour parvenir au
   niveau de sant \& eacute; sexuelle le plus \& eacute;lev \& eacute;
   possible, et des environnements juridiques favorables sont essentiels
   pour progresser dans ce domaine. Lorsqu'on d \& eacute;termine
   l'alignement global sur les normes des droits de l'homme pour respecter,
   prot \& eacute;ger et r \& eacute;aliser les droits relatifs \& agrave;
   la sant \& eacute; sexuelle sans discrimination, de nombreux aspects des
   lois, notamment leur sp \& eacute;cificit \& eacute; et contenu,
   influent sur les informations et services de sant \& eacute; sexuelle
   qui sont utilis \& eacute;s, lesquels sont restreints et pour qui. Afin
   de comprendre la nature des dispositions juridiques existantes
   concernant l'acc \& egrave;s \& agrave; l'information et aux services de
   sant \& eacute; sexuelle, nous avons analys \& eacute; le contenu de 40
   lois en anglais, en fran \& ccedil;ais et en espagnol dans 18 pays pour
   l'information et les services de sant \& eacute; sexuelle sp \&
   eacute;cifiques auxquels l'acc \& egrave;s est garanti ou interdit, et
   les dispositions de non-discrimination contenues dans ces lois. Dans
   l'ensemble, il existait de grandes variations entre pays dans les types
   de lois couvrant ces services ainsi que dans les types et le nombre de
   services et d'informations propos \& eacute;s. Certains pays englobaient
   diff \& eacute;rents services par le biais de plusieurs lois, et la
   plupart des lois consacr \& eacute;es sp \& eacute;cifiquement \&
   agrave; la sant \& eacute; sexuelle n'abordaient qu'un aspect restreint
   de la sant \& eacute; sexuelle et couvrait une petite gamme de services.
   Les caract \& eacute;ristiques prot \& eacute;g \& eacute;es dans les
   dispositions de non-discrimination et la sp \& eacute;cificit \& eacute;
   de ces dispositions par rapport aux services des sant \& eacute;
   sexuelle variaient \& eacute;galement. Ces observations peuvent \&
   eacute;clairer les dialogues juridiques et politiques nationaux autour
   de la sant \& eacute; sexuelle pour identifier les possibilit \&
   eacute;s de changement positif, ainsi que guider des recherches plus
   approfondies en vue de comprendre la relation entre ces dispositions
   juridiques, la mise en oe uvre de ces lois dans les pays et les r \&
   eacute;sultats pertinents en mati \& egrave;re de sant \& eacute;
   sexuelle.
   El acceso a informaci \& oacute;n y servicios de salud sexual es
   fundamental para alcanzar el m \& aacute;s alto nivel de salud sexual, y
   los entornos legislativos favorables son clave para lograr avances en
   esta \& aacute;rea. Para determinar la alineaci \& oacute;n general con
   las normas de derechos humanos de respetar, proteger y cumplir los
   derechos relacionados con la salud sexual sin discriminaci \& oacute;n,
   hay muchos aspectos de las leyes, tales como su especificidad y
   contenido, que influyen en qu \& eacute; informaci \& oacute;n y cu \&
   aacute;les servicios de salud sexual son aprovechados, cu \& aacute;les
   son restringidos y para qui \& eacute;n. Para entender la naturaleza de
   las disposiciones legislativas vigentes relativas al acceso a la
   informaci \& oacute;n y los servicios de salud sexual, analizamos el
   contenido de 40 leyes en ingl \& eacute;s, franc \& eacute;s y espa \&
   ntilde;ol de 18 pa \& iacute;ses para saber a qu \& eacute; informaci \&
   oacute;n y servicios espec \& iacute;ficos de salud sexual el acceso es
   garantizado o prohibido, y las disposiciones de no discriminaci \&
   oacute;n establecidas en estas leyes. En general, hubo gran variaci \&
   oacute;n entre pa \& iacute;ses en los tipos de leyes relativas a estos
   servicios y los tipos y la cantidad de servicios e informaci \& oacute;n
   garantizados. Algunos pa \& iacute;ses abarcaban diferentes servicios
   por medio de varias leyes, y la mayor \& iacute;a de las leyes dedicadas
   espec \& iacute;ficamente a la salud sexual abordaban solo un aspecto
   limitado de la salud sexual y una gama peque \& ntilde;a de servicios.
   Tambi \& eacute;n variaron las caracter \& iacute;sticas protegidas en
   las disposiciones de no discriminaci \& oacute;n y la especificidad de
   estas disposiciones con respecto a los servicios de salud. Los hallazgos
   podr \& iacute;an informar los di \& aacute;logos nacionales sobre leyes
   y pol \& iacute;ticas relativas a la salud sexual para identificar
   oportunidades de realizar cambios positivos, as \& iacute; como para
   guiar m \& aacute;s investigaciones a fin de entender la relaci \&
   oacute;n entre tales disposiciones legislativas, la aplicaci \& oacute;n
   de estas leyes en los pa \& iacute;ses y los resultados de salud sexual
   relevantes.},
